1
00:00:00,746 --> 00:00:02,976
One morning, you woke up.

2
00:00:03,247 --> 00:00:06,057
There was a number above everyone's head.

3
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,160
Not their age.

4
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:08,630
Not their IQ.

5
00:00:08,652 --> 00:00:10,802
How many more times you'd see them,

6
00:00:10,822 --> 00:00:12,382
in your whole life.

7
00:00:12,612 --> 00:00:13,847
You looked in the mirror.

8
00:00:13,867 --> 00:00:15,472
Nothing above your own head.

9
00:00:15,785 --> 00:00:16,743
You went outside.

10
00:00:16,763 --> 00:00:20,005
On the subway, everyone had the same number:

11
00:00:20,028 --> 00:00:22,548
1. You'll never see them again.

12
00:00:22,819 --> 00:00:26,479
The baker on the corner: 2,140.

13
00:00:26,709 --> 00:00:30,379
The coworker you never liked: 3,900.

14
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:33,270
You never chose the people you'd see the most.

15
00:00:33,790 --> 00:00:35,557
That day, your mom called.

16
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:37,548
"Coming over Sunday?"

17
00:00:37,568 --> 00:00:39,450
"We'll see," you said.

18
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:40,741
You went anyway.

19
00:00:40,761 --> 00:00:43,350
When she opened the door, it said 17.

20
00:00:43,663 --> 00:00:44,666
You did the math.

21
00:00:44,686 --> 00:00:47,095
Two holidays a year, plus her birthday.

22
00:00:47,115 --> 00:00:48,233
It was right.

23
00:00:48,504 --> 00:00:50,488
That evening she said, "Stay the night."

24
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:52,654
"I've got work tomorrow," you said.

25
00:00:52,718 --> 00:00:55,588
When the door closed, the number became 16.

26
00:00:56,191 --> 00:00:59,081
We all think the people we love will always be there.

27
00:00:59,103 --> 00:01:01,653
So we always leave them for last.

28
00:01:01,966 --> 00:01:04,195
Your daughter had 6,400.

29
00:01:04,215 --> 00:01:07,826
But as she grew up, it dropped faster.

30
00:01:07,849 --> 00:01:09,259
School. College.

31
00:01:09,279 --> 00:01:11,899
Another city.

32
00:01:12,046 --> 00:01:14,368
In the years she wanted to see you most,

33
00:01:14,388 --> 00:01:16,366
you were looking at your phone.

34
00:01:16,720 --> 00:01:18,551
Then you saw your dad.

35
00:01:18,571 --> 00:01:20,710
Above his head: 1.

36
00:01:20,733 --> 00:01:22,161
You sat next to him.

37
00:01:22,181 --> 00:01:24,333
He talked about the weather,

38
00:01:24,353 --> 00:01:26,923
the game, the price of tomatoes.

39
00:01:26,946 --> 00:01:29,217
You wanted to say something big.

40
00:01:29,237 --> 00:01:30,126
You couldn't.

41
00:01:30,356 --> 00:01:33,086
On your way out, you turned back...

42
00:01:33,106 --> 00:01:33,736
0.

43
00:01:34,711 --> 00:01:36,717
One Sunday night, you couldn't sleep.

44
00:01:36,737 --> 00:01:40,151
You opened your contacts and scrolled down.

45
00:01:40,174 --> 00:01:42,245
Next to every name, a number.

46
00:01:42,265 --> 00:01:43,804
You stopped at one.

47
00:01:44,075 --> 00:01:45,334
Your best friend from school.

48
00:01:45,354 --> 00:01:48,135
You never went a day without talking.

49
00:01:48,158 --> 00:01:49,238
You didn't fight.

50
00:01:49,258 --> 00:01:51,258
Nothing happened.

51
00:01:51,281 --> 00:01:52,590
You just didn't call.

52
00:01:52,610 --> 00:01:53,864
Neither did he.

53
00:01:53,884 --> 00:01:55,841
Life filled the space.

54
00:01:55,863 --> 00:01:58,003
He didn't even know you'd lost your dad.

55
00:01:58,275 --> 00:01:59,682
Next to his name:

56
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:01,408
9. A few weddings.

57
00:02:01,428 --> 00:02:03,371
A few coincidences.

58
00:02:03,391 --> 00:02:04,455
That's it.

59
00:02:04,726 --> 00:02:05,770
You typed.

60
00:02:05,790 --> 00:02:07,521
Deleted. Then sent:

61
00:02:07,541 --> 00:02:09,706
"Coffee this weekend?"

62
00:02:09,770 --> 00:02:11,767
30 seconds later, a reply.

63
00:02:11,787 --> 00:02:13,605
Like he'd been waiting for years:

64
00:02:13,625 --> 00:02:15,230
"Finally! Yes!"

65
00:02:15,584 --> 00:02:17,658
When you saw him that weekend,

66
00:02:17,678 --> 00:02:19,955
the number wasn't 9 anymore.

67
00:02:19,975 --> 00:02:21,244
It was 150.

68
00:02:21,971 --> 00:02:23,909
Those numbers weren't fate.

69
00:02:23,929 --> 00:02:25,891
Just a prediction.

70
00:02:25,914 --> 00:02:28,964
Change what you do, and the number changes too.

71
00:02:29,235 --> 00:02:30,880
That night, you called your mom.

72
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,991
"I'm coming this Sunday," you said.

73
00:02:33,011 --> 00:02:34,985
"And the Sunday after."

74
00:02:35,381 --> 00:02:37,160
You looked in the mirror again.

75
00:02:37,180 --> 00:02:38,941
Still nothing above your head.

76
00:02:38,964 --> 00:02:41,018
Because that number shows how many more

77
00:02:41,038 --> 00:02:42,844
times others will see you.

78
00:02:42,991 --> 00:02:44,791
And you can never see it.

79
00:02:45,476 --> 00:02:47,667
The first person who comes to mind right

80
00:02:47,687 --> 00:02:50,476
now... what number is above their head?

81
00:02:50,706 --> 00:02:51,907
Make it bigger.

82
00:02:51,927 --> 00:02:55,356
Today. Then write their name in the comments.

